  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INCREASING LOCAL CAPACITY FOR CLIMATE CHANGE MITIGATION AND ADAPTATION TO LOSS AND DAMAGE IN BAYELSA STATE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This response is to build the capacity of stakeholders in Bayelsa communities vulnerable to perennial flooding and coastal erosion to avoid the impact of climate change. The project hopes to achieve this objectives through advocacy, capacity building and livelihood restoration through media and community engagement. The intervention will take place at Igbogene community of Yenoaga, the administrative headquarters of Bayelsa state, south-south Nigeria which is vulnerable to every negative impact of global climate changes.</narrative>
  </description>
